# --- Community ---
# The Discord invite is referenced ONLY here. Everything else — the /comicreader/ hero
# badge, the iOS/Android apps, the App Store description, the NAS distribution README —
# links to bibliofuse.com/discord instead, so a dead invite is a one-line fix in one repo
# rather than a hunt through every place the code was pasted.
#
# UWKcJ4uMMQ was generated 2026-09-10 with Expire after: Never and no use limit
# (verified: the invites API returns expires_at: null). The invite it replaced was a
# 30-day default that would have 404'd on 2026-10-10.
#
# Invites also die from channel changes, not just expiry: this one is bound to
# #announcement, so deleting, renaming or restricting that channel breaks the link.
#
# 302, not 301, on purpose. Browsers cache a 301 indefinitely, so anyone who clicked once
# would keep being sent to the old invite from their own cache after we changed it here —
# which defeats the entire point of the indirection. Every other rule in this file points
# at a permanent destination and correctly uses 301; this one is expected to change.
/discord           https://discord.gg/UWKcJ4uMMQ  302
/discord/          https://discord.gg/UWKcJ4uMMQ  302
/:lang/discord     https://discord.gg/UWKcJ4uMMQ  302
/:lang/discord/    https://discord.gg/UWKcJ4uMMQ  302
